// DuckDB filters, groups, and aggregates the rows: the `where` and the
// `summarize` go into the query. The result equals that of
// `table_summarize_local.tql`, which aggregates the same rows locally. Only
// the local aggregation sees the row whose struct `meta` is null and warns
// about it, which shows that DuckDB computed this summary.
from_duckdb env("DUCKDB_SEED"), table="events"
where id > 1 or name == null
summarize ok, n=count(), names=count(name), first=min(id), latest=max(ts), meta.port=max(meta.port)
sort ok
